Alex,

Thanks for doing that! I'm assuming that tracing will only be useful with your help?

I've made some progress on my end. I took the vagrant file from the main renjin repo, and used that to eliminate any os setup issues.

By doing some smart commenting out, I've found which calls crash GCC:
 * calls to std::make_shared
 * calls to push_back on instances of std::vector are causing the crashes
 * calls to push on instances of std::priority_queue

Which is actually pretty impressive that it's only those calls, though the push_back method is surprising to me because it seems like a pretty common method.

Commenting out those usages seems to let it compile just fine. (well, there's a java error in the code gen side, but I'm hoping that goes away when I can uncomment those lines).

For reference, I've compiled my progress with the actual sources I'm using here: https://github.com/samsieber/jvm-fasttext and here's the commit where I comment out those problematic calls: https://github.com/samsieber/jvm-fasttext

Thanks for all your help thus far, I look forward to seeing what tracing reveals.

Sam.

